I come out of the clinic.
There is a medical store nearby.
The doctor's prescription is in my hand.
I should buy the medicine now.
I walk slowly and go inside the shop.
A man is standing at the counter.
I say to him, "Bhaiya, I need these medicines."
I give him the doctor's prescription.
He reads the prescription and turns around.
After a few minutes, he comes back.
He has tablets and a cough syrup in his hand.
He says, "Madam, these are your medicines."
"You should drink this syrup twice a day."
"And you should take these tablets after eating food."
I nod and ask, "How much is it?"
He says, "Two hundred and fifty rupees."
I give him the money and put the medicines in my bag.
I should go home quickly and rest now.
The medicine bag is now in my hand.
I walk slowly toward home.
